WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.107
Is geography about what makes

2
00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:03.704
each place unique,

3
00:00:03.704 --> 00:00:05.486
or about general laws?

4
00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:07.406
The discipline has swung both

5
00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:08.305
ways.

6
00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:09.526
In 1939,

7
00:00:09.526 --> 00:00:12.676
Hartshorne said geography studies how

8
00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:14.105
areas differ.

9
00:00:14.105 --> 00:00:14.861
In 1953,

10
00:00:14.861 --> 00:00:17.064
Fred Schaefer argued it should

11
00:00:17.064 --> 00:00:17.952
seek laws,

12
00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:20.989
opening the quantitative revolution.

13
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.063
Behavioural geographers studied how people

14
00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:25.177
perceive space.

15
00:00:25.177 --> 00:00:28.387
Radical geographers looked at inequality.

16
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:29.934
Humanistic geographers,

17
00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.846
at meaning and place.

18
00:00:32.177 --> 00:00:34.484
The syllabus also lists cultural

19
00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:37.294
regions and welfare approaches.

20
00:00:37.995 --> 00:00:39.266
Your turn.

21
00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:40.737
Who wrote it?
